module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.BaseAdicFiltration.AdicStageEndpoints
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Thickenings
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.SchemeDeformationConormal
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.Geometric.SpecialFibreIdealSheaf

/-!
# The special fibre of a first-order deformation is a first-order thickening

Let `A` be an object of `𝒞_Λ` and let `W` be a scheme over `baseSpec A` whose fibre over the
closed point is cut out by a cartesian square — a deformation in the sense of
[Stacks Project, Tag 0DY7], or either endpoint of a deformation of a morphism. The ideal sheaf
of that fibre is the ideal `𝔪_A 𝒪_W` generated by the maximal ideal of `A`
(`Deformation.Examples.ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback`), and taking the ideal generated by an
ideal of the base commutes with powers. So the special-fibre immersion is a **first-order
thickening** exactly when the maximal ideal of `A` has square zero, which for the dual numbers
`k[ε]` it does: the maximal ideal is the principal ideal `(ε)`.

This is the hypothesis `i.ker ^ 2 = ⊥` that [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2] carries, read on the base
object where it is a condition on `A` alone, and discharged at the dual-number object of `𝒞_Λ`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.ker_sq_eq_bot_of_isPullback`: the leg of a cartesian square over the
  closed point of `baseSpec A` is square-zero as soon as the maximal ideal of `A` is.
* `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_sq_eq_bot_of_dualNumberEquiv`: the maximal ideal of an
  object of `𝒞_Λ` carrying a dual-number coordinate has square zero.
* `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_artinianDualNumbers_sq_eq_bot`: the same for the
  dual-number object of `𝒞_Λ` itself, with the coordinate hypothesis discharged.
* `Deformation.Examples.isFirstOrderThickening_specialMap`: **the special-fibre immersion of a
  first-order deformation of a scheme is a first-order thickening.**

## Implementation notes

The hypothesis carried by the results below is an algebra isomorphism `A ≃ₐ[Λ] DualNumber k`
rather than an equality of objects of `𝒞_Λ`, exactly as in
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/SchemeDeformationConormal.lean`, and for the same
reason: an equality of base objects is not something the library transports along. Only the
ring structure of `A` enters, through its maximal ideal, and the isomorphism is discharged for
the intended object by `Deformation.Examples.artinianDualNumbersCoordinate`.

The transport of square-zeroness across that isomorphism is taken on the image ideal rather than
on the preimage: `IsLocalRing.map_ringEquiv_maximalIdeal` identifies the image of the maximal
ideal with the maximal ideal, `Ideal.map_pow` commutes the image with the square, and an ideal
whose image under an injective ring map is zero is zero. The square-zeroness of the maximal ideal
of `DualNumber k` is `DualNumber.maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton_eps` together with
`Ideal.span_singleton_pow`, `ε` squaring to zero.

No flatness is used: the ideal-sheaf computation is base change for closed immersions, which
holds for any cartesian square. In particular the statement applies to either endpoint of a
deformation of a morphism, whose special-fibre squares are
`Deformation.Examples.ker_specialSource` and `Deformation.Examples.ker_specialTarget`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CK2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04EX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04EX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

universe u

namespace Deformation.Examples

variable {Λ k : Type u} [CommRing Λ] [Field k] [Algebra Λ k]

/-- **A base change of the closed point of `baseSpec A` is square-zero when `𝔪_A` is.** The
ideal sheaf of the leg `i` of a cartesian square over `Deformation.Examples.residueSpecMap A` is
`𝔪_A 𝒪_W` by `Deformation.Examples.ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback`, and the ideal generated by
a power of an ideal of the base is the corresponding power. -/
theorem ker_sq_eq_bot_of_isPullback {A : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, u, u} Λ k} {W Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (pW : W ⟶ baseSpec A) {i : Z ⟶ W} {q : Z ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of k)}
    (h : IsPullback i q pW (residueSpecMap A))
    (hA : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (A : Type u) ^ 2 = ⊥) : i.ker ^ 2 = ⊥ := by
  rw [ker_eq_baseIdeal_of_isPullback pW h]
  exact Stacks.BaseAdicFiltration.baseIdeal_pow_eq_bot pW hA

/-- **The maximal ideal of an object of `𝒞_Λ` carrying a dual-number coordinate has square
zero.** The maximal ideal of `k[ε]` is the principal ideal `(ε)`, whose square is generated by
`ε²= 0`; an isomorphism of algebras carries the maximal ideal to the maximal ideal and commutes
with powers. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_sq_eq_bot_of_dualNumberEquiv {A : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, u, u} Λ k}
    (e : A ≃ₐ[Λ] DualNumber k) : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (A : Type u) ^ 2 = ⊥ := by
  have hmap : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (A : Type u)).map e.toRingEquiv =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (DualNumber k) :=
    IsLocalRing.map_ringEquiv_maximalIdeal e.toRingEquiv
  have hsq : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (DualNumber k)) ^ 2 = ⊥ := by
    rw [DualNumber.maximalIdeal_eq_span_singleton_eps, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
    simp
  have h2 : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (A : Type u) ^ 2).map e.toRingEquiv = ⊥ := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, hmap, hsq]
  exact (Ideal.map_eq_bot_iff_of_injective e.injective).mp h2

/-- **The maximal ideal of the dual-number object of `𝒞_Λ` has square zero**, the coordinate
hypothesis being discharged by `Deformation.Examples.artinianDualNumbersCoordinate`. -/
theorem maximalIdeal_artinianDualNumbers_sq_eq_bot :
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal
        ((Deformation.artinianDualNumbers.{u, u, u} Λ k : ArtinianLocalAlgCat.{u, u, u} Λ k) :
          Type u) ^ 2 = ⊥ :=
  maximalIdeal_sq_eq_bot_of_dualNumberEquiv artinianDualNumbersCoordinate

/-- **The special-fibre immersion of a first-order deformation of a scheme is a first-order
thickening.** It is a closed immersion by
`Deformation.Examples.deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion`, being a base change of the
closed point, and its ideal sheaf is square-zero because the maximal ideal of the base object
is, by `Deformation.Examples.maximalIdeal_sq_eq_bot_of_dualNumberEquiv`.

This is the hypothesis `i.ker ^ 2 = ⊥` of [Stacks Project, Tag 0CK2], discharged for the
deformations over the dual numbers to which [Stacks Project, Tag 0E3V] applies it. -/
@[stacks 0DY7 "the special-fibre immersion of a deformation over the dual numbers is a \
first-order thickening"]
theorem isFirstOrderThickening_specialMap {X : Over (Spec (CommRingCat.of k))}
    (P : SchemeDeformationCategory (Λ := Λ) (k := k) X)
    (coordinate : P.base ≃ₐ[Λ] DualNumber k) :
    Stacks.Thickenings.IsFirstOrderThickening P.specialMap :=
  ⟨deformationSpecialMap_isClosedImmersion P,
    ker_sq_eq_bot_of_isPullback P.toBase P.specialCartesian
      (maximalIdeal_sq_eq_bot_of_dualNumberEquiv coordinate)⟩

end Deformation.Examples

end
